{"body":"## Problem\n\nThe rules meant to hold mise-managed Python below 3.14 do not fire. `basher83/Zammad-MCP#306` is Renovate proposing `python 3.13.14 → 3.14.7` in `mise.toml` on a repo that extends `presets/python-mcp.json` and also carries its own `matchPackageNames: [\"python\"]` rule. The `requires-python` cap in `pyproject.toml` has held, so the failure is specific to the mise entries.\n\n## Cause (from Renovate source)\n\n`lib/modules/manager/mise/upgradeable-tooling.ts` defines the `python` tool as:\n\n```ts\npython: {\n  config: {\n    packageName: 'python/cpython',\n    datasource: GithubTagsDatasource.id,\n    extractVersion: '^v(?<version>\\\\S+)',\n  },\n},\n```\n\nand `lib/modules/manager/mise/extract.ts` builds the dependency with `depName: getConfiguredDepName(config) ?? name`, where `name` is the key in `mise.toml`. So for `python = \"3.13.14\"`:\n\n| field | value |\n| --- | --- |\n| `depName` | `python` |\n| `packageName` | `python/cpython` |\n| `datasource` | `…795 tokens truncated…the reported dependency fields and matcher behavior against the Renovate version used by the consumer.\n- Fix the mise Python caps in `presets/python-mcp.json` and `presets/ansible.json`, preserving the Docker cap behavior.\n- Validate the root configuration and all presets with `renovate-config-validator --strict`.\n- After the preset fix is available to the consumer, refresh the affected PR and confirm Python remains below 3.14; the expected remaining update from the report is `uv 0.12.20 → 0.12.21`.\n- Review the consumer's copied cap rule for removal once the shared preset covers it.\n\nTracking: BB task REN-1 creates this report; REN-3 covers claim verification and implementation. The diagnosis above is supplied by the task and has not been independently verified as part of issue creation.\n","number":120,"state":"OPEN","title":"fix(presets): Python cap rules for mise never match (matchPackageNames vs packageName)","url":"https://github.com/basher83/renovate-config/issues/120"}
"}

